1
00:00:01,126 --> 00:00:01,919
Previously on "Friends"...

2
00:00:01,961 --> 00:00:03,086
DON'T COME OUT HERE.

3
00:00:04,379 --> 00:00:07,090
YOU CANNOT TELL CHANDLER,
BUT I RAN INTO RICHARD.

4
00:00:07,132 --> 00:00:07,925
WHICH RICHARD?

5
00:00:07,967 --> 00:00:09,217
MY EX-BOYFRIEND RICHARD.

6
00:00:09,259 --> 00:00:10,385
THIS IS THE WORST THING

7
00:00:10,427 --> 00:00:11,762
THAT CAN HAPPEN
ON AN ANNIVERSARY.

8
00:00:11,804 --> 00:00:13,221
OH, GOOD. YOU DECIDED
TO TELL HIM

9
00:00:13,263 --> 00:00:14,765
ABOUT THE
RICHARD THING.

10
00:00:17,017 --> 00:00:19,353
OH, NO.

11
00:00:19,394 --> 00:00:21,188
YOU CANNOT SEE HIM
EVER AGAIN.

12
00:00:21,229 --> 00:00:22,523
YOU CAN'T TELL
ME WHAT TO DO.

13
00:00:22,564 --> 00:00:24,358
THAT'S SO FUNNY.

14
00:00:24,399 --> 00:00:25,609
I THINK
I JUST DID.

15
00:00:25,651 --> 00:00:28,111
I HAVE FOUND
MY IDENTICAL HAND TWIN.

16
00:00:28,153 --> 00:00:29,822
WHAT'S AN IDENTICAL
HAND TWIN?

17
00:00:29,864 --> 00:00:31,699
IT'S A GUY WITH
MY IDENTICAL HANDS.

18
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:33,367
I'M GOING TO BE
A MILLIONAIRE.

19
00:00:34,827 --> 00:00:35,870
YAY!

20
00:00:37,162 --> 00:00:38,622
YES, COME ON!

21
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:44,712
YOU ACTUALLY THOUGHT
I WANTED TO HAVE SEX WITH YOU?

22
00:00:44,753 --> 00:00:46,296
NO.

23
00:00:47,214 --> 00:00:49,758
LAST NIGHT WAS EMBARRASSING
FOR YOU, TOO.

24
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:52,427
I JUST DON'T EMBARRASS
THAT EASILY.

25
00:01:00,101 --> 00:01:02,563
I THINK THE CHECK-IN
IS THAT WAY.

26
00:01:02,604 --> 00:01:03,647
AH.

27
00:01:03,689 --> 00:01:04,857
( laughing )

28
00:01:04,899 --> 00:01:05,983
( laughs )

29
00:01:06,025 --> 00:01:07,985
HELLO!

30
00:01:09,528 --> 00:01:13,365
OH, KIDS LOVE ME.

31
00:01:13,407 --> 00:01:14,366
HEY!

32
00:01:14,408 --> 00:01:15,367
PHOEBE!

33
00:01:15,409 --> 00:01:16,535
YOU GUYS ARE HERE!

34
00:01:16,577 --> 00:01:17,745
YAY!

35
00:01:17,786 --> 00:01:20,205
WHAT'D YOU DO, GO
TO A COSTUME PARTY?

36
00:01:20,247 --> 00:01:22,123
LET ME GUESS.

37
00:01:22,165 --> 00:01:23,542
PANCHO VILLA.

38
00:01:23,584 --> 00:01:25,377
( chuckling )

39
00:01:25,419 --> 00:01:27,462
AND YOU'RE BOB SAGET.

40
00:01:29,673 --> 00:01:30,883
"PANCHO VILLA"?

41
00:01:30,925 --> 00:01:32,259
YEAH.

42
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:34,803
WHAT ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT,
PHEEBS? I DON'T...

43
00:01:34,845 --> 00:01:36,847
( gasps )

44
00:01:38,766 --> 00:01:39,934
OH, MY GOD!

45
00:01:39,975 --> 00:01:41,727
YOU DREW ON ME?

46
00:01:41,769 --> 00:01:43,478
HEY, YOU WET MY PANTS!

47
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:44,772
HEY...

48
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:46,648
WHOA, WHAT KIND
OF PARTY WAS THIS?

49
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:49,860
ROSS, I HAVE BEEN WALKING AROUND
LIKE THIS SINCE THE PLANE?

50
00:01:49,902 --> 00:01:51,403
YOU HAVE SO CROSSED A LINE.

51
00:01:51,445 --> 00:01:52,404
RACH, WAIT.

52
00:01:52,446 --> 00:01:54,907
THE MEN'S ROOM IS THAT WAY.

53
00:01:57,325 --> 00:01:58,744
( coins clinking )

54
00:01:58,786 --> 00:02:00,328
OH!

55
00:02:00,370 --> 00:02:01,663
WHAT?

56
00:02:01,705 --> 00:02:03,624
THAT'S, LIKE, THE THIRD
TIME THAT LADY'S WON

57
00:02:03,665 --> 00:02:04,917
ON A MACHINE
I WAS PLAYING.

58
00:02:04,959 --> 00:02:07,711
OH, I BET SHE'S
ONE OF THOSE PEOPLE.

59
00:02:07,753 --> 00:02:10,672
M-M-MOLE PEOPLE?

60
00:02:10,714 --> 00:02:12,841
WHAT? NO. NO, A LURKER.

61
00:02:12,883 --> 00:02:14,093
OH. WHAT'S A LURKER?

62
00:02:14,134 --> 00:02:16,344
OKAY, WHEN YOU'RE
PLAYING A MACHINE

63
00:02:16,386 --> 00:02:17,679
AND IT HASN'T PAID OUT

64
00:02:17,721 --> 00:02:20,265
A LURKER WAITS FOR YOU
TO GIVE UP AND THEN...

65
00:02:20,307 --> 00:02:21,558
KILLS YOU?

66
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:26,354
NO, THEY SWOOP IN
AND STEAL YOUR JACKPOT.

67
00:02:26,396 --> 00:02:27,815
OH.
MM-HMM.

68
00:02:27,856 --> 00:02:29,357
HOW DO YOU KNOW
ABOUT THIS?

69
00:02:29,399 --> 00:02:31,234
MY NANA USED
TO DO IT, MM-HMM.

70
00:02:31,276 --> 00:02:33,695
THAT'S HOW SHE PAID
FOR ALL MY DANCE...

71
00:02:33,737 --> 00:02:34,947
KARATE LESSONS.

72
00:02:34,989 --> 00:02:37,198
DANCE KARATE?

73
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:40,911
YES. IT'S A DEADLY
BUT BEAUTIFUL SPORT.

74
00:02:44,581 --> 00:02:45,791
OKAY

75
00:02:45,833 --> 00:02:47,250
IT WON'T COME OFF.

76
00:02:47,292 --> 00:02:48,293
WHAT?

77
00:02:48,335 --> 00:02:49,419
IT WON'T COME OFF.

78
00:02:49,461 --> 00:02:50,462
OH, MY GOD.

79
00:02:50,504 --> 00:02:52,047
RACH, ARE YOU SURE?

80
00:02:52,089 --> 00:02:54,508
NO. ACTUALLY, I TOOK IT OFF
AND THEN I DREW IT BACK ON.

81
00:02:55,676 --> 00:02:57,719
HEY, HEY!
YOU MADE IT!

82
00:02:57,761 --> 00:02:59,346
JOEY! HEY, HEY!

83
00:02:59,387 --> 00:03:00,555
HI.

84
00:03:00,597 --> 00:03:02,223
WHO'S YOUR FRIEND?
HE'S HOT.

85
00:03:02,265 --> 00:03:03,350
( chuckles )

86
00:03:03,391 --> 00:03:04,768
THANKS, MAN.

87
00:03:04,810 --> 00:03:07,395
HEY, LISTEN, I TALKED
TO CHANDLER.

88
00:03:07,437 --> 00:03:09,188
I'M SORRY ABOUT THE MOVIE.

89
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:10,524
DON'T BE SORRY.

90
00:03:10,565 --> 00:03:12,067
I DON'T NEED IT ANYMORE.

91
00:03:12,109 --> 00:03:14,069
I FOUND MY IDENTICAL HAND TWIN.

92
00:03:14,111 --> 00:03:15,779
YOUR WHAT?

93
00:03:15,821 --> 00:03:17,238
MY IDENTICAL HAND TWIN.

94
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,533
YEAH, THE PERSON WHOSE HANDS
ARE EXACTLY LIKE MINE.

95
00:03:19,574 --> 00:03:21,076
THIS THING
IS A GOLD MINE.

96
00:03:21,118 --> 00:03:22,077
WHAT?

97
00:03:22,119 --> 00:03:23,871
WHA...? HOW...?

98
00:03:23,912 --> 00:03:26,165
THAT'S NOT GOING
TO MAKE YOU ANY MONEY.

99
00:03:26,205 --> 00:03:27,708
OKAY. WELL, IF THAT'S
HOW YOU FEEL ABOUT IT, FINE.

100
00:03:27,749 --> 00:03:29,126
NONE OF YOU ARE GOING
TO GET TO LIVE WITH ME

101
00:03:29,168 --> 00:03:31,170
IN MY GREAT BIG
HAND-SHAPED MANSION.

102
00:03:33,130 --> 00:03:34,089
'CEPT YOU, PHEEBS.

103
00:03:34,131 --> 00:03:35,632
YOU CAN LIVE IN THE THUMB.

104
00:03:42,472 --> 00:03:47,728
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

105
00:03:47,769 --> 00:03:49,980
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

106
00:03:50,022 --> 00:03:52,607
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

107
00:03:52,649 --> 00:03:57,487
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

108
00:03:57,529 --> 00:04:00,074
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

109
00:04:00,115 --> 00:04:02,617
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

110
00:04:02,659 --> 00:04:06,538
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

111
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:10,209
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

112
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:18,550
ALL RIGHT, BABY, COME ON!

113
00:04:18,592 --> 00:04:19,927
YES! YES!
YES!

114
00:04:19,968 --> 00:04:21,220
I AM ON FIRE!

115
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:22,804
SEE YOU LATER, MON.

116
00:04:22,846 --> 00:04:24,973
CHANDLER, WHAT
ARE YOU DOING?

117
00:04:25,015 --> 00:04:26,850
WHAT DOES IT LOOK LIKE?
I'M GOING HOME.

118
00:04:26,892 --> 00:04:28,102
WAIT. WHY?

119
00:04:28,143 --> 00:04:30,104
CHANDLER?

120
00:04:30,145 --> 00:04:32,022
CHANDLER, LOOK.

121
00:04:32,064 --> 00:04:33,148
I'M SORRY.

122
00:04:33,190 --> 00:04:35,067
I WAS JUST PLAYING
FOR ONE SECOND.

123
00:04:35,109 --> 00:04:37,027
I WAS TRYING TO FIND YOU
AND TELL YOU THAT...

124
00:04:37,069 --> 00:04:39,487
LOOK, IF YOU DON'T WANT ME
TO SEE RICHARD AGAIN, I WON'T.

125
00:04:39,529 --> 00:04:40,530
HE MEANS NOTHING TO ME.

126
00:04:40,572 --> 00:04:41,865
OH, COME ON.

127
00:04:41,907 --> 00:04:43,242
I WAS THERE.

128
00:04:45,077 --> 00:04:47,537
I KNOW HE'S THE LOVE
OF YOUR LIFE.

129
00:04:47,579 --> 00:04:50,124
NOT ANYMORE.

130
00:04:50,165 --> 00:04:52,500
REALLY?

131
00:04:52,542 --> 00:04:54,335
REALLY.

132
00:04:57,881 --> 00:04:59,424
ALL RIGHT?

133
00:04:59,466 --> 00:05:01,468
LET'S FORGET ABOUT THIS
"GOING HOME" STUFF

134
00:05:01,509 --> 00:05:03,428
AND START CELEBRATING
OUR ANNIVERSARY.

135
00:05:04,638 --> 00:05:06,640
OKAY, THIS IS EMPTY.

136
00:05:06,681 --> 00:05:09,059
YEAH, I WANTED TO MAKE
A DRAMATIC SCENE

137
00:05:09,101 --> 00:05:10,811
BUT I HATE PACKING.

138
00:05:10,852 --> 00:05:12,187
( chuckles )

139
00:05:14,189 --> 00:05:16,900
UH, HEY, WHERE'S
THE OTHER GUY?

140
00:05:16,942 --> 00:05:18,401
WHICH GUY?

141
00:05:18,443 --> 00:05:19,694
HE'S KIND OF TALL, DARK HAIR

142
00:05:19,736 --> 00:05:21,280
HAND LOOKS
EXACTLY LIKE THIS, SEE?

143
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:22,614
I DON'T KNOW
ABOUT THE HANDS

144
00:05:22,656 --> 00:05:24,324
BUT THE GUY WHO WAS
HERE BEFORE ME

145
00:05:24,365 --> 00:05:25,575
JUST WENT
TO THE RESTROOM.

146
00:05:25,617 --> 00:05:26,994
OKAY.

147
00:05:32,207 --> 00:05:34,084
HOW YOU DOING?

148
00:05:34,126 --> 00:05:35,919
VERY BUSY.

149
00:05:35,961 --> 00:05:37,545
ALL RIGHT! OKAY!

150
00:05:41,716 --> 00:05:44,761
YES, HELLO, I
HAVE A QUESTION.

151
00:05:44,803 --> 00:05:49,641
UM, I USED YOUR PEN TO
DRAW ON MY FRIEND'S FACE.

152
00:05:49,683 --> 00:05:52,144
A BEARD AND A MUSTACHE.

153
00:05:52,186 --> 00:05:54,353
( chuckles )

154
00:05:54,395 --> 00:05:56,231
THANK YOU.

155
00:05:58,483 --> 00:06:00,819
NO, SHE DIDN'T THINK SO.

156
00:06:00,861 --> 00:06:01,987
I KNOW. IT'S, LIKE...

157
00:06:02,029 --> 00:06:03,030
ANYWAY, UM...

158
00:06:04,447 --> 00:06:07,117
MAKEUP DIDN'T COVER IT
AND WE'VE TRIED EVERYTHING

159
00:06:07,159 --> 00:06:09,410
TO GET IT OFF
AND NOTHING'S WORKED.

160
00:06:09,452 --> 00:06:10,787
WHAT DO WE DO?

161
00:06:10,829 --> 00:06:12,247
YEAH.

162
00:06:12,289 --> 00:06:15,709
UH-HUH... YEAH.

163
00:06:15,750 --> 00:06:17,376
OH, OKAY.

164
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:18,461
OKAY, THANK YOU.

165
00:06:19,462 --> 00:06:21,506
YEAH, IT'S NOT COMING OFF.

166
00:06:21,548 --> 00:06:22,924
WHAT?

167
00:06:22,966 --> 00:06:24,259
WHAT ELSE DID HE SAY?

168
00:06:24,301 --> 00:06:27,721
UM, HE SAID HE THOUGHT
I WAS FUNNY, SO...

169
00:06:29,306 --> 00:06:34,102
OKAY, LOOK, LOOK, LET'S JUST GO
DOWNSTAIRS, WE'LL HAVE SOME FUN

170
00:06:34,144 --> 00:06:36,355
AND YOU WILL FORGET
ALL ABOUT IT.

171
00:06:36,395 --> 00:06:37,939
ROSS, NO!

172
00:06:37,981 --> 00:06:40,275
THERE IS NO WAY I AM LEAVING
THIS ROOM LOOKING LIKE THIS.

173
00:06:40,317 --> 00:06:41,943
OH, COME ON, RACH,
IT'S NOT THAT BAD.

174
00:06:41,985 --> 00:06:44,196
ROSS, I AM
A HUMAN DOODLE!

175
00:06:44,238 --> 00:06:46,823
LOOK, JUST BECAUSE
SOME IDIOT DREW
ON YOUR FACE

176
00:06:46,865 --> 00:06:49,450
DOESN'T MEAN YOU
SHOULDN'T HAVE
ANY FUN, OKAY?

177
00:06:49,492 --> 00:06:50,785
BESIDES-- HEY, HEY, HEY

178
00:06:50,827 --> 00:06:53,163
NO ONE'S GOING TO EVEN
LOOK AT YOU, OKAY?

179
00:06:53,205 --> 00:06:54,455
THIS IS VEGAS, HELLO?

180
00:06:54,497 --> 00:06:56,415
THERE ARE TONS OF
OTHER FREAKS HERE.

181
00:06:57,792 --> 00:07:01,922
THERE ARE TONS OF
FREAKS HERE, NO OTHER.

182
00:07:01,963 --> 00:07:05,967
COME ON. NO ONE WILL
NOTICE, I SWEAR.

183
00:07:06,009 --> 00:07:07,177
COME ON.

184
00:07:12,974 --> 00:07:15,852
OKAY, THERE WAS
SOME STARING AND POINTING.

185
00:07:15,894 --> 00:07:19,106
OKAY, I NEED, I NEED A DRINK.

186
00:07:19,147 --> 00:07:21,400
HEY, YOU KNOW,
THEY REALLY OVERCHARGE YOU

187
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:22,442
FOR THAT STUFF.

188
00:07:24,152 --> 00:07:27,239
BUT WHO CARES,
BECAUSE IT'S ALL ON ME.

189
00:07:27,281 --> 00:07:28,823
( bottles clinking )

190
00:07:31,868 --> 00:07:34,413
THAT IS ONE BIG DRINK.

191
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:37,374
MACADAMIA NUT?

192
00:07:37,416 --> 00:07:38,375
UM, WOW!

193
00:07:38,417 --> 00:07:40,335
THAT'S, THAT'S SOME PRICEY NUT.

194
00:07:40,377 --> 00:07:42,045
MM.

195
00:07:42,087 --> 00:07:44,923
YOU REALLY LIKE THOSE
MACADAMIA NUTS, HUH?

196
00:07:44,965 --> 00:07:46,425
NOPE.

197
00:07:58,061 --> 00:08:00,855
GET OUT OF HERE,
YOU LURKER!

198
00:08:00,897 --> 00:08:02,190
GO ON, GET!

199
00:08:02,232 --> 00:08:04,025
( coin clinks )

200
00:08:04,067 --> 00:08:05,026
HEY, PHEEBS.

201
00:08:05,068 --> 00:08:07,195
YOU MADE UP.

202
00:08:07,237 --> 00:08:09,906
YEAH, I COULDN'T BE
MAD AT HIM FOR TOO LONG.

203
00:08:09,948 --> 00:08:12,075
YEAH, SHE COULDN'T LIVE
WITHOUT THE CHAND-LOVE.

204
00:08:16,079 --> 00:08:17,247
OKAY, GET A ROOM.

205
00:08:17,289 --> 00:08:19,498
WE HAVE ONE.

206
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:20,583
I KNOW. USE IT.

207
00:08:24,212 --> 00:08:26,214
OH, YEAH.

208
00:08:26,256 --> 00:08:28,049
THAT'S RIGHT.

209
00:08:28,091 --> 00:08:30,135
YOU TAKE GOOD CARE
OF THOSE BABIES.

210
00:08:30,177 --> 00:08:31,719
EXCUSE ME?

211
00:08:31,761 --> 00:08:32,929
IT'S ME, JOEY.

212
00:08:32,971 --> 00:08:34,389
DO I KNOW YOU?

213
00:08:34,431 --> 00:08:37,892
JOEY...

214
00:08:37,934 --> 00:08:39,478
OH, YEAH.

215
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:42,897
YEAH, THE HAND GUY.

216
00:08:42,939 --> 00:08:44,774
OKAY, SO, WHAT ARE
WE GOING TO DO

217
00:08:44,816 --> 00:08:46,401
ABOUT THIS HAND
TWIN THING?

218
00:08:46,443 --> 00:08:48,903
NOTHING.

219
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:52,740
LOOK, YOU AND I HAVE
BEEN GIVEN A GIFT, OKAY?

220
00:08:52,782 --> 00:08:54,284
WE HAVE TO DO
SOMETHING WITH IT

221
00:08:54,326 --> 00:08:55,576
LIKE HAND MODELING, HUH?

222
00:08:55,618 --> 00:08:56,995
OR MAGIC.

223
00:08:57,037 --> 00:09:00,040
AND YOU KNOW NASA's GOING
TO WANT TO TALK TO US.

224
00:09:00,081 --> 00:09:02,042
I HAVE TO GET
BACK TO WORK.

225
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:03,793
WHOA, WHOA, WHOA!

226
00:09:03,835 --> 00:09:05,837
WE COULD HAVE OUR
OWN SHOW, YOU KNOW?

227
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:07,672
WE COULD CLAP OUR
HANDS TOGETHER.

228
00:09:07,714 --> 00:09:09,049
PEOPLE WILL LOVE IT

229
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:10,842
HUH?

230
00:09:10,884 --> 00:09:12,677
AND I WROTE A SONG
FOR US.

231
00:09:12,719 --> 00:09:16,431
♪ THIS HAND IS YOUR HAND ♪

232
00:09:16,473 --> 00:09:19,851
♪ THIS HAND IS MY HAND ♪

233
00:09:19,893 --> 00:09:22,187
♪ OH, WAIT, THAT'S YOUR HAND ♪

234
00:09:23,730 --> 00:09:25,982
♪ NO, WAIT. IT'S MY HAND. ♪

235
00:09:26,024 --> 00:09:27,025
SEE?

236
00:09:27,067 --> 00:09:29,861
THAT'S OKAY.

237
00:09:29,903 --> 00:09:32,739
BUT YOU HAVEN'T EVEN
HEARD THE CHORUS!

238
00:09:34,949 --> 00:09:36,451
OH, MY GOD.

239
00:09:36,493 --> 00:09:39,287
I'M STARTING TO LOOK
LIKE MY GREAT-AUNT MURIEL.

240
00:09:39,329 --> 00:09:41,331
ALL RIGHT, YOU KNOW WHAT?

241
00:09:41,373 --> 00:09:43,917
WE DON'T HAVE TO GO DOWNSTAIRS.

242
00:09:43,958 --> 00:09:47,128
WE CAN BRING VEGAS UP TO US.

243
00:09:47,170 --> 00:09:48,922
ALL RIGHT, COME ON. COME ON.

244
00:09:48,963 --> 00:09:51,174
LET'S GO. WE'LL PLAY
SOME BLACKJACK.

245
00:09:51,216 --> 00:09:52,175
HERE WE GO. 13.

246
00:09:52,217 --> 00:09:52,800
HIT ME.

247
00:09:52,842 --> 00:09:55,554
OOH, 23.

248
00:09:56,513 --> 00:10:00,141
WHICH IS WHAT WE PLAY TO
AT THIS CASINO.

249
00:10:02,060 --> 00:10:03,978
YOU WIN TEN DOLLARS.

250
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:04,812
I BET $20.

251
00:10:04,854 --> 00:10:08,149
RIGHT.

252
00:10:08,191 --> 00:10:10,277
( people clamoring )

253
00:10:11,486 --> 00:10:14,948
A NEW PAIR OF SHOES
FOR THE CHAN-CHAN MAN.

254
00:10:14,989 --> 00:10:16,283
YES!

255
00:10:16,324 --> 00:10:19,160
I'VE NEVER SEEN A ROLL
LIKE THIS IN MY LIFE!

256
00:10:19,202 --> 00:10:20,454
THAT'S RIGHT, BABY!

257
00:10:20,495 --> 00:10:22,163
OKAY, WHAT DO
I WANT NOW?

258
00:10:22,205 --> 00:10:24,374
OKAY, UH, AN EIGHT.

259
00:10:24,416 --> 00:10:26,251
UH, A SIX.

260
00:10:26,293 --> 00:10:27,252
PICK A NUMBER!

261
00:10:27,294 --> 00:10:28,503
THAT IS YOUR ONLY JOB!

262
00:10:28,545 --> 00:10:29,546
EIGHT, EIGHT.

263
00:10:29,588 --> 00:10:30,547
THANK YOU.

264
00:10:30,589 --> 00:10:31,881
OKAY, IF YOU
GET THIS ONE

265
00:10:31,923 --> 00:10:33,967
WE BUY EVERYBODY
HERE A STEAK DINNER.

266
00:10:34,008 --> 00:10:35,718
( all cheer )

267
00:10:36,761 --> 00:10:37,804
Croupier:
EIGHT AGAIN.

268
00:10:37,845 --> 00:10:38,805
YES! YES!

269
00:10:38,846 --> 00:10:40,098
WE AREN'T REALLY GOING

270
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:42,016
TO BUY THESE PEOPLE
STEAK DINNERS, ARE WE?

271
00:10:42,058 --> 00:10:43,017
NO.

272
00:10:43,059 --> 00:10:44,018
OKAY, GOOD.

273
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:46,104
OKAY, WHAT DO I WANT NOW?

274
00:10:46,146 --> 00:10:47,730
UH, TRY A HARD EIGHT.

275
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:49,065
WHAT?
TWO FOURS.

276
00:10:49,107 --> 00:10:50,108
OKAY.

277
00:10:50,150 --> 00:10:51,318
Croupier:
EIGHT THE HARD WAY.

278
00:10:51,359 --> 00:10:52,611
YES!

279
00:10:52,651 --> 00:10:54,237
DON'T YOU LET HER GO.

280
00:10:54,279 --> 00:10:55,780
YOU'RE A LUCKY GUY.

281
00:10:55,822 --> 00:10:58,658
THANK YOU,
MR. DRUNKEN GAMBLER.

282
00:10:58,699 --> 00:10:59,951
OKAY, YOU GET THIS

283
00:10:59,993 --> 00:11:02,454
AND WE GET THE BIGGEST
SUITE IN THE PLACE.

284
00:11:02,496 --> 00:11:05,373
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT, WAIT.

285
00:11:05,415 --> 00:11:07,375
WE GET THE BIGGEST
SUITE IN THE PLACE.

286
00:11:07,417 --> 00:11:08,668
( all groan )

287
00:11:08,709 --> 00:11:10,587
ALL RIGHT, THE BIGGEST SUITE
IN THE PLACE.

288
00:11:10,629 --> 00:11:12,713
COME ON.

289
00:11:12,755 --> 00:11:14,174
YES! I LOVE YOU!

290
00:11:14,215 --> 00:11:16,717
I CAN'T EVEN REMEMBER
WHAT WE WERE FIGHTING ABOUT.

291
00:11:16,759 --> 00:11:18,595
THAT'S 'CAUSE I HAD
LUNCH WITH RI...

292
00:11:18,637 --> 00:11:19,887
ME, NEITHER!

293
00:11:19,929 --> 00:11:21,222
OKAY, WHAT DO I WANT NOW?

294
00:11:21,264 --> 00:11:22,223
ANOTHER HARD EIGHT.

295
00:11:22,265 --> 00:11:23,308
"HARD EIGHT"?

296
00:11:23,350 --> 00:11:24,976
YOU SHOULD CALL IT
"EASY EIGHT."

297
00:11:25,018 --> 00:11:26,478
OKAY, OKAY,
I'LL TELL YOU WHAT.

298
00:11:26,520 --> 00:11:28,146
YOU ROLL ANOTHER
HARD EIGHT...

299
00:11:28,188 --> 00:11:31,399
AND WE GET MARRIED
HERE TONIGHT.

300
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:35,903
COME ON, ROLL!

301
00:11:35,945 --> 00:11:38,906
SHUT UP!

302
00:11:40,908 --> 00:11:43,286
IT JUST GOT INTERESTING!

303
00:11:49,042 --> 00:11:50,627
WHAT DID YOU JUST SAY?

304
00:11:50,669 --> 00:11:52,086
YOU ROLL ANOTHER
HARD EIGHT

305
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:53,880
AND WE GET MARRIED
HERE TONIGHT.

306
00:11:53,921 --> 00:11:55,714
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

307
00:11:55,756 --> 00:11:57,716
YES. I LOVE YOU.

308
00:11:57,758 --> 00:12:00,554
I'VE NEVER LOVED ANYBODY
AS MUCH AS I LOVE YOU.

309
00:12:00,595 --> 00:12:04,140
I'VE NEVER LOVED ANYBODY
AS MUCH AS I LOVE YOU.

310
00:12:04,182 --> 00:12:06,351
OKAY, SO IF AN
EIGHT COMES UP

311
00:12:06,393 --> 00:12:08,228
WE TAKE IT AS A SIGN
AND WE DO IT.

312
00:12:08,269 --> 00:12:09,479
WHAT DO YOU SAY?

313
00:12:09,521 --> 00:12:10,980
OKAY!

314
00:12:11,022 --> 00:12:12,065
OKAY.

315
00:12:12,106 --> 00:12:13,983
HARD EIGHT.

316
00:12:14,025 --> 00:12:15,776
( everyone cheering )

317
00:12:16,777 --> 00:12:17,987
( disappointed groans )

318
00:12:18,029 --> 00:12:19,322
OKAY, THAT'S A FOUR!

319
00:12:19,364 --> 00:12:21,366
AND WHERE... WHERE...
WHERE'S THE OTHER ONE?

320
00:12:21,408 --> 00:12:22,450
IT WENT UNDER THE TABLE.

321
00:12:22,492 --> 00:12:23,784
NOBODY MOVE!

322
00:12:23,826 --> 00:12:26,287
OKAY, YOU LOOK THAT WAY,
I'LL LOOK THIS WAY!

323
00:12:30,709 --> 00:12:33,378
HERE IT IS.
HERE IT IS.

324
00:12:33,420 --> 00:12:35,630
THAT COULD BE
A FOUR OR A FIVE.

325
00:12:37,465 --> 00:12:40,009
IT'S YOUR CALL.

326
00:12:43,346 --> 00:12:45,724
IT'S A FOUR.

327
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:50,311
I THINK SO, TOO.

328
00:13:16,795 --> 00:13:19,591
OH, WELL. LOST AGAIN.

329
00:13:23,928 --> 00:13:24,887
THAT'S IT!

330
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:26,389
YOU AND ME, OUTSIDE!

331
00:13:26,431 --> 00:13:28,141
I WOULDN'T WANT
TO SEE YOU LOSE

332
00:13:28,182 --> 00:13:30,143
A CHUNK OF THAT
PRETTY BLOND HAIR.

333
00:13:32,771 --> 00:13:34,481
OH!

334
00:13:34,522 --> 00:13:37,191
BE COOL. BE COOL.

335
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:40,069
( quietly conversing )

336
00:13:40,111 --> 00:13:42,572
OKAY, LADY, YOUR LURKING DAYS
ARE OVER.

337
00:13:42,614 --> 00:13:43,822
WHAT?!
YEAH.

338
00:13:43,864 --> 00:13:45,241
FROM NOW ON, EVERYONE YOU LURK

339
00:13:45,283 --> 00:13:46,367
I'M GOING TO LURK FIRST.

340
00:13:46,409 --> 00:13:47,744
IF YOU MOVE ON TO SOMEONE ELSE

341
00:13:47,786 --> 00:13:49,496
I'M GOING TO BE
ONE STEP AHEAD OF YOU

342
00:13:49,537 --> 00:13:51,038
EVERY SINGLE TIME.

343
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:54,833
AND THEN I'LL BE ON YOUR ASS
EVERY HOUR OF EVERY DAY...

344
00:13:54,875 --> 00:13:56,461
TILL MONDAY.

345
00:13:56,503 --> 00:13:59,673
'CAUSE THAT'S WHEN I GO HOME.

346
00:13:59,714 --> 00:14:00,923
WHEN DO YOU LEAVE?

347
00:14:00,965 --> 00:14:02,634
ALSO MONDAY.

348
00:14:02,676 --> 00:14:03,760
WHAT TIME?

349
00:14:03,802 --> 00:14:05,178
MAYBE WE CAN SHARE A CAB.

350
00:14:07,138 --> 00:14:09,349
HIT ME.

351
00:14:09,390 --> 00:14:11,559
HIT ME.

352
00:14:11,601 --> 00:14:12,477
HIT ME.

353
00:14:13,645 --> 00:14:15,271
HIT ME.

354
00:14:15,313 --> 00:14:16,648
HIT ME.

355
00:14:18,232 --> 00:14:19,108
HIT ME.

356
00:14:19,150 --> 00:14:20,860
( heavy sigh )

357
00:14:20,901 --> 00:14:22,362
WE NEED MORE CARDS.

358
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:26,032
YEAH, AND WE ALSO NEED
MORE, UM, DRINKS.

359
00:14:26,073 --> 00:14:27,408
HOLD ON A SECOND.

360
00:14:28,409 --> 00:14:30,662
WOOP. OKAY.

361
00:14:30,704 --> 00:14:32,664
HELLO, VEGAS? YEAH.

362
00:14:34,081 --> 00:14:37,293
WE WOULD LIKE SOME MORE ALCOHOL
AND YOU KNOW WHAT ELSE?

363
00:14:37,335 --> 00:14:39,086
WE WOULD LIKE SOME MORE BEERS.

364
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:41,005
WHA...? HELLO?

365
00:14:41,047 --> 00:14:44,008
OH, I FORGOT TO DIAL.

366
00:14:45,510 --> 00:14:46,761
( knocking on door )

367
00:14:46,803 --> 00:14:50,014
THAT MUST BE OUR ALCOHOL
AND BEERS.

368
00:14:54,561 --> 00:14:55,687
HEY.
HEY, IT'S JOEY!

369
00:14:55,729 --> 00:14:57,856
I LOVE JOEY!

370
00:14:57,938 --> 00:14:59,816
Rachel:
OH, I LOVE JOEY!

371
00:14:59,858 --> 00:15:01,401
OH, JOEY LIVES WITH A DUCK.

372
00:15:01,442 --> 00:15:02,485
HI!

373
00:15:02,527 --> 00:15:03,695
OKAY.

374
00:15:03,737 --> 00:15:05,363
ALL RIGHT, LOOK, LOOK,
LOOK, YOU GUYS.

375
00:15:05,405 --> 00:15:06,406
I NEED SOME HELP, OKAY?

376
00:15:06,447 --> 00:15:07,615
SOMEONE HAS GOT
TO HELP ME

377
00:15:07,657 --> 00:15:09,325
CONVINCE MY HAND TWIN
TO COOPERATE.

378
00:15:09,367 --> 00:15:11,202
I'LL DO IT.

379
00:15:11,244 --> 00:15:13,705
HEY, WHATEVER YOU NEED
ME TO DO, I'M YOUR MAN.

380
00:15:13,747 --> 00:15:15,248
HEY.

381
00:15:17,458 --> 00:15:19,168
WHOA... WHOA... WHOA.

382
00:15:19,210 --> 00:15:21,295
ARE YOU... ARE YOU OKAY?

383
00:15:23,673 --> 00:15:25,925
YEAH. FINE. THANKS.

384
00:15:28,845 --> 00:15:30,263
HEY, RACH.

385
00:15:30,304 --> 00:15:32,473
HOW YOU DOIN'?

386
00:15:34,642 --> 00:15:38,271
I'M DOIN' GOOD, BABY.
HOW YOU DOIN'?

387
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:39,647
YEAH.

388
00:15:39,689 --> 00:15:41,524
ROSS, DON'T LET HER DRINK
ANYMORE.

389
00:15:44,026 --> 00:15:45,194
OH...

390
00:15:45,236 --> 00:15:49,156
HERE'S THAT MACADAMIA NUT.

391
00:15:49,198 --> 00:15:50,450
OH.

392
00:15:50,491 --> 00:15:52,118
NOPE. SOMETHING ELSE.

393
00:15:52,159 --> 00:15:53,119
OOPS.

394
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:56,497
( Rachel laughing )

395
00:15:58,833 --> 00:16:00,835
ALL RIGHT, SO WHAT DO YOU WANT
TO DO NOW?

396
00:16:00,877 --> 00:16:02,670
I WANT TO GET OUT OF
THE ROOM.

397
00:16:02,712 --> 00:16:04,839
I... YOU KNOW, I...

398
00:16:04,881 --> 00:16:07,133
I REALLY MISS DOWNSTAIRS.

399
00:16:07,174 --> 00:16:08,175
MMM.

400
00:16:08,217 --> 00:16:10,177
OKAY, YOU KNOW WHAT?

401
00:16:10,219 --> 00:16:13,514
THERE IS ONLY ONE WAY I AM
LEAVING THIS HOTEL ROOM.

402
00:16:14,641 --> 00:16:16,601
WELL, HELLO.

403
00:16:16,643 --> 00:16:17,936
HI. WELCOME TO VEGAS.

404
00:16:17,977 --> 00:16:19,938
I'M ROSS.

405
00:16:19,978 --> 00:16:20,939
GOOD LUCK TO YOU.

406
00:16:20,979 --> 00:16:22,148
EXCUSE ME, SIR.

407
00:16:22,189 --> 00:16:23,858
YOU'VE GOT A LITTLE
SOMETHING RIGHT...

408
00:16:23,900 --> 00:16:25,902
( both laughing )

409
00:16:28,070 --> 00:16:29,155
OH.
WOW.

410
00:16:29,196 --> 00:16:30,323
HELLO.

411
00:16:30,364 --> 00:16:31,658
HELLO.

412
00:16:31,699 --> 00:16:35,244
HELLO.
HELLO.

413
00:16:35,286 --> 00:16:36,871
( meowing ):
HELLO.

414
00:16:53,847 --> 00:16:55,014
NO! OH!

415
00:16:58,100 --> 00:16:59,268
WHOO!

416
00:16:59,310 --> 00:17:00,812
I WON!

417
00:17:00,854 --> 00:17:02,814
I WON! I FINALLY WON!

418
00:17:02,856 --> 00:17:04,774
I WON! THAT WAS MY QUARTER!

419
00:17:04,816 --> 00:17:06,108
HERE. TAKE A HIKE, TOOTS.

420
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:08,027
( gasping )

421
00:17:08,068 --> 00:17:10,029
EXCUSE ME, SIR.

422
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:11,531
THIS LADY PLAYED
MY QUARTER.

423
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:12,907
THIS IS MY MONEY.

424
00:17:12,949 --> 00:17:14,450
IS THAT TRUE, MISS?

425
00:17:14,492 --> 00:17:17,411
( mumbling ):
UM... SELLS DRUGS TO KIDS.

426
00:17:17,453 --> 00:17:18,788
WHAT?

427
00:17:18,830 --> 00:17:21,624
SHE SELLS DRUGS TO KIDS.

428
00:17:22,917 --> 00:17:24,961
IT WAS MY QUARTER.

429
00:17:25,003 --> 00:17:26,504
WAS IT HER QUARTER?

430
00:17:26,546 --> 00:17:29,883
HOW ABOUT WE TALK ABOUT THIS
OVER DINNER, HUH?

431
00:17:29,924 --> 00:17:31,885
OKAY, LADY, YOU'RE
OUT OF HERE.

432
00:17:31,926 --> 00:17:33,803
NO, NO, YOU
CAN'T ARREST ME!

433
00:17:33,845 --> 00:17:36,138
NO, I WON'T GO BACK!
I WON'T GO BACK TO
THAT HELLHOLE!

434
00:17:37,431 --> 00:17:40,393
I'M JUST TAKING YOU OUTSIDE.

435
00:17:40,434 --> 00:17:41,936
OH, OKAY.

436
00:17:44,355 --> 00:17:46,148
Monica:
OKAY, COME ON, I
CAN'T GET MARRIED

437
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:47,984
UNTIL I GET SOMETHING
OLD, SOMETHING NEW

438
00:17:48,026 --> 00:17:49,736
SOMETHING BORROWED
AND SOMETHING BLUE.

439
00:17:49,777 --> 00:17:50,737
OKAY, OKAY.

440
00:17:50,778 --> 00:17:52,030
ALL RIGHT,
ALL RIGHT. OKAY.

441
00:17:52,071 --> 00:17:54,490
OKAY, HERE'S SOMETHING
BLUE AND NEW.

442
00:17:54,532 --> 00:17:56,200
YOU ARE SO EFFICIENT.

443
00:17:56,242 --> 00:17:57,201
I LOVE YOU.

444
00:17:57,243 --> 00:17:58,202
LET'S GO.

445
00:17:58,244 --> 00:17:59,245
NO, NO, NO, WAIT!

446
00:17:59,286 --> 00:18:00,580
WE NEED SOMETHING OLD.

447
00:18:00,621 --> 00:18:03,416
UH, OKAY... I HAVE A
CONDOM IN MY WALLET

448
00:18:03,457 --> 00:18:05,418
THAT I'VE HAD
SINCE I WAS 12.

449
00:18:05,459 --> 00:18:07,461
THAT'LL WORK.

450
00:18:07,503 --> 00:18:10,089
I DON'T THINK SO.

451
00:18:10,130 --> 00:18:12,759
OKAY, NOW WE JUST NEED
SOMETHING BORROWED.

452
00:18:14,052 --> 00:18:16,136
HERE, JUST TAKE THIS.

453
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:18,264
THAT'S STEALING.

454
00:18:18,305 --> 00:18:19,599
WE'LL... WE'LL BRING IT BACK.

455
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:20,975
JUST PUT IT UNDER YOUR DRESS.

456
00:18:28,066 --> 00:18:30,068
AW.

457
00:18:32,528 --> 00:18:34,655
OKAY, ONE THING AT A TIME.

458
00:18:43,497 --> 00:18:45,291
( groaning )

459
00:18:46,084 --> 00:18:47,710
ARE YOU GOING TO PLAY?

460
00:18:47,752 --> 00:18:49,420
NO, NO. I DON'T REALLY
HAVE ANY MONEY.

461
00:18:49,462 --> 00:18:51,422
( chuckling )

462
00:18:51,464 --> 00:18:54,383
NOT YET, ANYWAY. HUH?

463
00:18:54,425 --> 00:18:57,470
CAN'T SIT HERE IF YOU'RE
NOT GOING TO PLAY.

464
00:18:57,511 --> 00:18:59,472
ALL RIGHT.

465
00:19:03,726 --> 00:19:05,019
OH, YEAH.

466
00:19:05,061 --> 00:19:08,481
OH, HOO-HOO-HOO-HOO.

467
00:19:08,522 --> 00:19:10,942
OH...

468
00:19:10,984 --> 00:19:12,693
HELLO.

469
00:19:12,735 --> 00:19:15,613
MY NAME IS REGINA FILANGIE.

470
00:19:17,281 --> 00:19:20,158
I'M A BUSINESSWOMAN
IN TOWN ON BUSINESS.

471
00:19:20,200 --> 00:19:21,995
WOULD YOU LIKE TO SEE MY CARD?

472
00:19:22,036 --> 00:19:24,038
OH, WHAT DID I DO
WITH MY FILOFAX?

473
00:19:24,080 --> 00:19:26,582
I MUST'VE LEFT IT IN
CONFERENCE ROOM "B."

474
00:19:26,624 --> 00:19:28,375
FOURTEEN.

475
00:19:28,417 --> 00:19:29,919
HIT ME.

476
00:19:29,961 --> 00:19:31,129
OH, MY GOD.

477
00:19:31,169 --> 00:19:33,255
MAY I JUST SAY THAT
YOU TWO GENTLEMEN

478
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:35,758
HAVE THE EXACT SAME HANDS?

479
00:19:35,800 --> 00:19:36,550
( Joey gasping )

480
00:19:36,592 --> 00:19:38,636
THEY'RE IDENTICAL.

481
00:19:38,678 --> 00:19:41,555
NOW, I'VE NEVER SEEN ANYTHING
LIKE THAT IN THE BUSINESS WORLD.

482
00:19:42,932 --> 00:19:45,643
STOP IT.

483
00:19:45,685 --> 00:19:47,020
MISS FILANGIE?

484
00:19:47,061 --> 00:19:48,688
MAY I ASK YOU A QUESTION

485
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:50,690
AS AN IMPARTIAL PERSON
AT THIS TABLE?

486
00:19:50,731 --> 00:19:53,026
PLEASE STOP IT.

487
00:19:53,067 --> 00:19:55,736
HUH... UH, WOULDN'T
YOU PAY GOOD MONEY

488
00:19:55,778 --> 00:19:58,447
TO SEE THESE IDENTICAL
HANDS SHOWCASED

489
00:19:58,489 --> 00:20:01,909
IN SOME TYPE OF A, UH,
ENTERTAINMENT VENUE, HUH?

490
00:20:01,951 --> 00:20:06,039
IF YOU LEAVE NOW, I WILL CHOP
OFF MY HAND AND GIVE IT TO YOU.

491
00:20:08,833 --> 00:20:10,751
DIDN'T I JUST THROW
YOU OUT OF HERE?

492
00:20:10,793 --> 00:20:12,753
NO, YOU THREW OUT PHOEBE.

493
00:20:12,795 --> 00:20:14,505
I'M REGINA FILANGIE.

494
00:20:14,547 --> 00:20:16,132
FILANGIE.

495
00:20:16,174 --> 00:20:18,509
COME ON, LADY.

496
00:20:18,551 --> 00:20:20,053
PLEASE... PLEASE TAKE HIM, TOO.

497
00:20:20,094 --> 00:20:21,470
ME?! OH, COME ON, MAN.

498
00:20:21,512 --> 00:20:22,930
FORGET ABOUT IT,
BUDDY. COME ON.

499
00:20:22,972 --> 00:20:25,683
WHOA, WHOA, WHOA, WHOA!

500
00:20:25,725 --> 00:20:27,643
DON'T LET HIM DO THIS! COME ON!

501
00:20:27,685 --> 00:20:30,437
I'M YOUR HAND TWIN!

502
00:20:34,358 --> 00:20:36,569
HELLO. ONE MARRIAGE, PLEASE.

503
00:20:36,610 --> 00:20:38,738
YEP. WE WANT
TO GET MARRIED.

504
00:20:38,779 --> 00:20:40,406
WELL, THERE'S A
SERVICE IN PROGRESS.

505
00:20:40,447 --> 00:20:41,407
HAVE A SEAT.

506
00:20:41,448 --> 00:20:43,201
ALL RIGHT.
ALL RIGHT.

507
00:20:45,745 --> 00:20:47,621
( humming "Pomp and
Circumstance" )

508
00:20:52,085 --> 00:20:53,293
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

509
